WHY NOT AN OPEN SOURCE LICENCE

The Open Source Definition, clause 6, forbids a licence from restricting use in
any field of endeavour. This licence restricts commercial use, so it is not an
open source licence and does not claim to be.

That is a deliberate choice, and the curriculum makes the argument in its own
text. Open source and Indigenous data governance agree on a great deal and
disagree on one thing: whether a community may set terms on what is done with
its own material. We have chosen the same side Te Hiku Media chose when they
wrote the Kaitiakitanga License rather than picking one off the shelf.

